            <ArticleTitle>Rechargeable Sodium All-Solid-State Battery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acscentsci.6b00321</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A reversible plating/stripping of a dendrite-free metallic-sodium anode with a reduced anode/ceramic interfacial resistance is created by a thin interfacial interlayer formed in situ or by the introduction of a dry polymer film. Wetting of the sodium on the interfacial interlayer suppresses dendrite formation and growth at different discharge/charge C-rates. All-solid-state batteries were obtained with a high cycling stability and Coulombic efficiency at 65 °C.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
